{"description":"`eka init` writes the EKA standard declaration file (root `EKA`, compact consumer summary, `Version X.Y` line) into the generated repository. The file is vendored from the eka-standard GitHub release asset (github.com/maleolabs/eka-standard, releases/download/v1.0/EKA) into an embed package (root-level //go:embed, ADR-023 pattern) and copied by the bootstrap engine — init stays offline and dry-run stays deterministic. Requires an ADR-020 amendment (Decision 1 carve-out: identity-only + standard declaration file) and an ADR-023 position note (embed mechanism revived for cross-repo canonical source distribution). `standardVersion` in cmd/version.go is derived from the embedded file instead of the hardcoded const (standard-corpus axis of sto:version-clarity, ~13 render sites follow mechanically). Build-time version-consistency test: the embedded `Version X.Y` line must equal the standard version the CLI conformance rules implement.","acceptanceCriteria":"Generated repository contains the EKA file with the correct `Version X.Y` line. Dry-run plans `generate file: EKA` deterministically (same bytes every run). Re-run on an already-initialized EKA repository backfills the EKA file when missing; identical content is reused; differing content follows the overwrite-confirm/skip contract. Bootstrap contains no network code (init remains offline). Build-time test fails when the embedded version line differs from the supported standard version. standardVersion renders from the embedded file — no hardcoded const remains. ADR-020 amended and ADR-023 note recorded. All existing init tests (cmd/execute_test.go) still pass."}